> Second one: Shopkeeper calling out know your race even if he can't see
> you and never saw you:

This is one of the tricky issues facing me at the moment.

Shopkeepers do _not_ come to their doors right now.  There are some very
good reasons for this, not the least of which being "need to stay out of
the way so the player can enter."

With this behavior in place *and* the "don't get in the line of fire
through the door" behavior when you approach the door, shopkeepers generally 
can't see you until you actually enter their shop.

So, if I used line of sight to trigger their yelling, I'd have wasted time
adding it in the first place; they'd never say a word.  For now, let's
just assume that shopkeepers have a "sixth sense" regarding money, and
when a potential customer approaches, they have found ways to know.

